      "settlementKey": "bravelyn:Solthéra",
      "description": "High Confessor Tektus is a Half-Orc confessor with a sermon voice like a locked gate and a talent for turning doubt into treason. From the Solthera Watch Office, he guards doctrine, interrogates dissent, and shapes The Choral Synod policy around obedience, purity, and the useful fear of outside corruption. He is charismatic, insecure, authoritarian, and far more dangerous when he smiles than when he threatens.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Solthéra is a Village in Bravelyn, under Gerontocracy, with moderate danger, Beach and reefs with water, Ocean Surface floating settlement, Beach and grass with water terrain. Local records favor Neutral, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Elf — Sea Elf, Tortle, Genasi — Water Genasi. Half-Orc reads through the Human entry of the race compendium, within Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, marked by Nebyrr. The local form is read through Half-Orc (Human + Orc Lineage). Humans are highly adaptable and found in nearly every environment across the world. They are known for their cultural diversity, short generational cycles, and unmatched versatility among mortal races. Table cues: Resourceful, Skillful, Versatile; starting tendency Neutral - Neutral - Neutral - Neutral.",
      "rumors": [
        "High Confessor Tektus knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Anubaday.",
        "High Confessor Tektus has a contact in Greenhollow Plains who will deny everything."
